      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A well-framed approach is to introduce a section in the presentation that transparently addresses analytical rigor and quality control measures that are intrinsic to the research process. First, you can explain the data screening and cleaning protocols that are part of the standard operating procedure. This includes steps for error detection and correction to ensure the integrity of the clinical trial data.\n\nYou should follow this with a discussion of the analytical process, including the steps taken to assess data quality and the reasons that led to the exclusion of certain data points. For instance, you can state that, following a thorough review of all Batch #77 data and strict adherence to the diagnostic criteria for sensor artifacts, the data team found one signal that was an outlier, substantially deviating from the expected response pattern due to a technical anomaly—a situation not previously encountered in the clinical trial process.\n\nThen, address the procedural appropriateness of retaining ten out of twelve patient data points, ensuring you clarify that this course of action was driven by statistical reasoning and not arbitrariness, providing the necessary context around why all the data from the twelve patients was nonetheless relevant and foundational to the analysis. This way, you’re positioning the exclusion as a necessary adjustment to an unexpected and rare occurrence.\n\nMoreover, since you know the",
